description:
crate-jmap-calendars-server/src/memory.rs:80 declares 'pub struct MemoryError(pub String);' — a tuple struct with a public String field.

The canonical jmap-mail-server (since commit 2941c50) and jmap-filenode-server (since e9b66a3) use a forward-compat shape:

  #[non_exhaustive]
  pub struct MemoryError { description: String }
  impl MemoryError {
      pub fn new(impl Into<String>) -> Self { ... }
      pub fn description(&self) -> &str { ... }
  }
  impl Display for MemoryError { write self.description }

This is a canonical-template divergence. The propagation rule (workspace AGENTS.md 'Canonical Templates' + this crate's AGENTS.md banner) requires this crate to mirror jmap-mail-server's shape.

Maintenance consequence: every future consumer who studies this MemoryBackend as 'the reference impl' learns a non-forward-compat error shape and copies it. The struct's pub field is also part of MemoryBackend's public API, so changing it later is a SemVer break.

Same fix pattern as bd:JMAP-filenode-server commit e9b66a3 — about 8 construction sites in src/memory.rs (line 417, 435, 676, 684, 737).

Sibling sweep candidates: also check tasks/chat/metadata before bundling.
